.Dd August 23, 2026
.Dt LIBCAPBUNDLE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm libcapbundle
.Nd parse and validate capability bundles
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libcapbundle
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In libcapbundle.h
.Ft int
.Fn capbundle_open "const char *path" "struct capbundle **bp" "char *errbuf" "size_t errlen"
.Ft void
.Fn capbundle_close "struct capbundle *b"
.Ft int
.Fn capbundle_verify "const struct capbundle *b" "char *errbuf" "size_t errlen"
.Ft int
.Fn capbundle_scan_dir "const char *path" "capbundle_scan_cb cb" "void *arg"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
parses the two-level capability bundle format used by
.Xr serviced 8 .
A bundle has one
.Pa Bundle.ucl
and an exact inventory of
.Pa Units/name.unit/Unit.ucl
process manifests and
.Pa Units/name.unit/bin/name
executables.
Identity, publisher metadata, version ordering, and shared storage are bundle
fields; activation, process policy, storage grants, local descriptors, and
capabilities are unit fields.
.Pp
Parsing is literal and closed.
Unknown or duplicate keys, includes, macros, variables, implicit arrays,
invalid names, incompatible network claims, ambiguous storage, and entries
beyond fixed limits are rejected.
Activation is explicit under
.Va activation.boot ,
.Va activation.ipc ,
.Va activation.timer
.Pq an object with a monotonic Va interval in seconds ,
.Va activation.schedule
.Pq a calendar cron string or named alias, optionally with Va persistent ,
.Va activation.path
.Pq an object with an absolute Va path watched for change events ,
.Va activation.queue_directory ,
.Va activation.on_mount ,
and
.Va activation.socket .
A monotonic
.Va timer
and a wall-clock
.Va schedule
are mutually exclusive.
Local authority replacements are typed entries in
.Va descriptors ;
the filesystem descriptor must name storage with mount rights.
.Pp
.Fn capbundle_verify
checks the exact tree shape, executable type and mode, activation triggers,
name uniqueness, and resource limits.
.Sh ACCESSORS
The public header exposes immutable accessors for bundle identity, display
version, sequence, author, publisher, path, unit count, unit labels,
activation, IPC names, timer interval, activation path, arguments,
environment, storage, descriptors, and conversion to
.Vt struct svc_manifest .
Returned strings remain owned by the bundle.
.Sh TRUST
.Nm
rejects symlinks and special objects but does not establish ownership policy.
.Xr serviced 8
requires registry trees to be root-owned and not group/world writable.
.Xr servicectl 8
normalizes and atomically publishes staged installations.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Functions returning
.Vt int
return zero on success and -1 on failure.
When supplied, the error buffer receives an administrative diagnostic.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr serviced 5 ,
.Xr serviced 8 ,
.Xr servicectl 8
